        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lyons%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s post office began operations in 1870, just a year after the town was laid out.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lyons%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early settlers in the 1870s built the first church, the Hicks Cumberland Presbyterian Church, marking the start of organized worship in Lyons.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lyons%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Lyons sits in southwestern Indiana, about 30 miles southeast of Terre Haute and 85 miles southwest of Indianapolis.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
